description:
Replaces live dual-running. Open throwaway PRs based on the flip branch (ci.yml has no branch filter, so they get CI; close all unmerged afterwards):
- one trivial change per unit (core, explorer, results-data, docs, landing, tooling) -> only that unit runs, other five pass as untouched;
- one PR touching core + docs + explorer -> three units run;
- one PR touching a soundness path -> soundness flag fails without the `Soundness review:` section, passes with it;
- one deliberately broken change per unit (failing test, lint error, broken build, invalid bundle, broken docs build, broken landing link) -> that unit's result job fails.
Also run the flip branch's merge_group behavior once via workflow_dispatch or a test merge-group-equivalent run of T2 to confirm the job budget (<=8 jobs) and wall time.
